WEBVTT

00:14:56.117 --> 00:15:00.376
before I take the plunge
into the writing burrow

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.106
but not while I'm in it.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.525
AG: How do you prevent
that from happening?

00:15:04.549 --> 00:15:06.596
Is there a mental firewall of sorts?

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:09.373
MA: You turn it off.

00:15:10.397 --> 00:15:12.492
AG: For many people,
easier said than done.

00:15:12.516 --> 00:15:14.268
You just turn it off and that's it?

00:15:14.292 --> 00:15:15.863
MA: Just don't go there.

00:15:16.934 --> 00:15:19.891
AG: It can help to schedule
a specific task in your calendar,

00:15:19.915 --> 00:15:21.836
the same way you schedule meetings.

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:23.034
In one experiment,

00:15:23.058 --> 00:15:26.276
writers were randomly assigned
to plan daily writing sessions.

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:28.606
They were over four times more productive,

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:31.086
and they didn't lose any creativity.